# Literal adaptation (docs/spec/06-conversions.md 8.1) reaches ARRAY-LITERAL
# elements whenever the destination is an array type. the loops-cleanup plan.
#
# The fixed-size half already did this -- `d: [3]u32 = [1, 2, 3]` has compiled
# since 1.6, because src/tychoc.c:6757 pushed the destination's element type
# into each element. The DYNAMIC half did not: `a: [u32] = [1, 2]` synthesized
# `[int]` and died "declared type [u32] but value is [int]", so the only way to
# build a `[u32]` from literals was `a := []u32` followed by `push(a, 1)`. That
# asymmetry was the defect; the two forms now take the same path.
fn main():
    a: [u32] = [1, 2]
    b: [float] = [1, 2]        # int literals adapt to float, element-wise
    c: [f32] = [1.0, 2.0]
    d: [3]u32 = [1, 2, 3]      # the fixed form, unchanged
    e: bounded[4]u32 = [1, 2]  # the bounded form, unchanged
    println(str(to_int(a[0]) + to_int(a[1])))
    println(str(b[0] + b[1]))
    println(str(to_int(c[0]) + to_int(c[1])))
    println(str(to_int(d[2])))
    println(str(to_int(e[1])))
    println(str(len(a)))
